-- `target/profraw-census/<utc>-<pid>/`, or `target/profraw-census/<name>/` when the script is given a name (one path segment; `.` and `..` are refused): the per-run tallies `scripts/profraw-census.sh <runs> <workers> [<name>]` writes, gitignored. The script is a dev-host witness for the corrupt-profile mechanism (test-plan §10 Stack adjustments): it runs the root bin's start test `<runs>` times over `<workers>` loops on the newest instrumented test binary under `target/llvm-cov-target/debug/deps/`, with a per-run `LLVM_PROFILE_FILE` prefix it sets inside itself, counts and sizes each run's profiles and removes them. Its last line is `profraw-census: runs N · passed N · profiles P · third K · short S`; it exits 0 only when every run passed, P equals N and K and S are 0, 1 on any other count, and 2 on a usage error or with no instrumented binary. No CI job, `pre-push` stage or harness command runs it.
+- `target/profraw-census/<utc>-<pid>/`, or `target/profraw-census/<name>/` when the script is given a name (one path segment; `.` and `..` are refused): the per-run tallies `scripts/profraw-census.sh <runs> <workers> [<name>]` writes, gitignored. The script is a dev-host witness for the corrupt-profile mechanism (test-plan §10 Stack adjustments): it runs the root bin's start test `<runs>` times over `<workers>` loops on the newest instrumented test binary under `target/llvm-cov-target/debug/deps/`, with a per-run `LLVM_PROFILE_FILE` prefix it sets inside itself, counts and sizes each run's profiles and removes them. Its last line is `profraw-census: runs N · passed N · profiles P · third K · short S`; it exits 0 only when every run passed, P equals N and K and S are 0, 1 on any other count, and 2 on a usage error or with no instrumented binary. Its second form, `--case <binary stem> <test name> <runs> <workers> [<name>]`, runs one integration case of the same instrumented build the same way, names each profile with its binary signature (`r<i>-%p-%<nproc>m.profraw`), offers each one alone to the toolchain's `llvm-profdata merge`, keeps a refused one under `refused/` and ends `profraw-census: runs N · passed N · profiles P · refused R`: exit 0 only when every run passed and R is 0, 1 otherwise, and 2 on a usage error or with no instrumented binary or no `llvm-profdata`. No CI job, `pre-push` stage or harness command runs either form.
